<h1 class="fs-37 lh-37 mb-24">Cards</h1>
<p class="mb-32">The original vertical blog card and a horizontal variant share the same image, post title, author, date, and excerpt.</p>
<h2 class="fs-24 lh-32 mb-16">Vertical card</h2>
<p class="mb-24">The card keeps its original <code>max-width: 344px</code> and shrinks with the available space. Both the card and its image use <code>border-r-16</code>.</p>
{% set markup %}{% include "components/cards/vertical.njk" %}{% endset %}
{{ example(markup, "Vertical blog card") }}
<h2 class="fs-24 lh-32 mb-16">Horizontal card</h2>
<p class="mb-24">The same image and content use a column on small screens and a row from 820 pixels up, with <code>flex-col</code>, <code>md-flex-row</code>, and <code>gap-24</code>.</p>
{% set horizontal %}{% include "components/cards/horizontal.njk" %}{% endset %}
{{ example(horizontal, "Horizontal blog card") }}
<p class="mb-24">This example preserves the original sample post links. The sample blog page is not included in this site, so replace those links when using the card in your project.</p>
<p><a href="/docs/images/">Image utilities</a> · <a href="/docs/colors/">Colors and palettes</a></p>
